{
  "description": "SASRec predicts the next item using causal self-attention over a user's interaction history. Item and position embeddings pass through attention and feed-forward blocks; the resulting features score candidate items through shared item embeddings. Training uses shifted next-item targets and sampled negatives. [Paper](https://arxiv.org/html/1808.09781v1)",
  "motivation": "Attention lets the model emphasize recent actions in sparse histories while using longer-range context when useful. This is relevant to categories with different interaction densities. Despite the supplied title, standard SASRec does not solve cold start for users without histories or items without training interactions. [Paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/1808.09781)",
  "implementation_notes": "Start from RecHarness sasrec_perdataset and preserve routing for all four categories. Keep preprocessing seed 0, training seed 42, DATA_DIR = os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'], and the SASREC_EPOCHS environment default of 200. Select configurations using only the pinned macro validation HR@10. Save artifacts beneath the trial directory and update the predictor writer whenever architecture changes. Retain DiagnosisProbe(view, device), run_full_diagnosis(train_loader), and diagnosis_interpreter_prompt(raw_diagnosis), reporting measured metrics with definitions. No task-specific improvement has been measured.",
  "pseudocode": "for category in four_categories:\n    load unchanged RecHarness splits\n    initialize category SASRec with training seed 42\n    for epoch in configured_epochs:\n        for _, sequence, positive, negative in train_loader:\n            features = model.log2feats(sequence)\n            pos_logits = score(features, positive)\n            neg_logits = score(features, negative)\n            loss = masked_mean(softplus(-pos_logits) + softplus(neg_logits))\n            optimize(loss)\n        evaluate through pinned validation protocol\n        save eligible checkpoint beneath trial directory\nselect configuration by macro validation HR@10\nwrite working/predict.py with matching architecture and category routing",
  "originality": {
    "score": 2,
    "positive": "The original paper introduced an influential application of self-attention to sequential recommendation.",
    "negative": "For this task, SASRec is already the prescribed baseline; the supplied idea adds no distinct cold-start mechanism."
  },
  "future_potential": {
    "score": 6,
    "positive": "Category-specific regularization and sequence-length tuning are plausible extensions. Public titles and descriptions could support a separately evaluated cold-start extension.",
    "negative": "Benefits remain unmeasured, and interaction-only embeddings provide limited support for unseen items."
  },
  "code_difficulty": {
    "score": 4,
    "positive": "The existing baseline and compatibility interface reduce implementation work.",
    "negative": "Correct padding and causal masks, predictor parity, diagnostic compatibility, and budget-aware validation still require care."
  }
}
